<h1>Engines</h1>


<section class="panel">
  <h2>Which one do you need?</h2>
  <p>The crew needs exactly <b>one</b> way to reach a model. Everything else on
  this page is optional. Pick by how you want to pay for it:</p>
  <ul class="rules">
    <li><b>You already pay for Claude.</b> Run <code>claude</code> in a terminal
      and log in once. Nothing to paste here, and no key is stored anywhere.</li>
    <li><b>You want the simplest start.</b> Get an OpenRouter key and paste it
      below. It reports what every call costs, which is why the crew's own
      spending figures are honest.</li>
    <li><b>Your company already pays for an assistant</b> and would never
      approve an outbound key. Point CostCrew at that tool on this machine:
      the spend stays on the contract you already have.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="fine">Without any of them the console still works completely: every
  figure is real, and agent runs say plainly that no engine is connected rather
  than inventing an analysis.</p>
</section>


<section class="panel">
  <h2>A subscription you already pay for</h2>
  
  <div class="engine">
    <div class="ehead">
      <b>Claude (subscription CLI)</b>
      
        <span class="chip st-todo">not checked</span>
        
      
    </div>

    <p class="ewhen">You already pay for Claude and want the crew to use that, with no key stored anywhere.</p>
    <p class="fine"><b>Cost:</b> Comes out of your Claude subscription, not a separate bill. A deep analysis is roughly USD 0.30-0.60 of usage.</p>
    <p class="fine"><b>How:</b> Run `claude` in a terminal, then `/login`, once. Nothing to paste here.
      <a href="https://claude.com/claude-code" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Open its page</a>.</p>

    
    
    <form method="post" action="/settings/recheck" class="inline"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<CSRF>">
      <button class="btn back">Check now</button>
    </form>
    <p class="fine">The check is a real model call and takes a few seconds, so
    opening this page never runs one.</p>
    
  </div>
  
</section>

<section class="panel">
  <h2>Your organisation&#39;s own assistant, on this machine</h2>
  
  <div class="engine">
    <div class="ehead">
      <b>Kiro CLI (headless)</b>
      
        <span class="chip st-blocked">not found on this machine</span>
        
      
    </div>

    <p class="ewhen">Your organisation already pays for Kiro and routes it through its own gateway. Nothing leaves this machine and no key is stored.</p>
    <p class="fine"><b>Cost:</b> Whatever your organisation already pays. CostCrew adds nothing, and cannot read what a run cost, so those runs are recorded as cost UNKNOWN rather than as free.</p>
    <p class="fine"><b>How:</b> Install Kiro and sign in once. Confirm the command with `kiro-cli chat --help`, since it changes between versions.
      <a href="https://kiro.dev" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Open its page</a>.</p>

    
    
    <form method="post" action="/settings/command" class="erow"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<CSRF>">
      <input type="hidden" name="provider" value="kiro">
      <input name="command" class="sel" spellcheck="false"
             value="kiro-cli chat --no-interactive {prompt}"
             placeholder="for example: kiro-cli chat --no-interactive {prompt}">
      <button class="btn">Update</button>
    </form>
    <p class="fine">No key is stored: the tool's own sign-in is the credential.
    Put <code>{prompt}</code> where the question should go; leave it out and it
    is appended at the end. The command is checked against this machine before
    it is saved, so a typo is caught here rather than mid-sprint.</p>

    
    
  </div>
  
  <div class="engine">
    <div class="ehead">
      <b>Any local agent CLI</b>
      
        <span class="chip st-todo">no command set</span>
      
    </div>

    <p class="ewhen">Any other tool on this machine that takes a prompt and prints an answer: Gemini CLI, Codex, an internal wrapper.</p>
    <p class="fine"><b>Cost:</b> Whatever that tool already costs you. Runs are recorded as cost UNKNOWN, never as free.</p>
    <p class="fine"><b>How:</b> Type the command below. Use {prompt} where the question should go, or leave it out and it is appended at the end.
      </p>

    
    
    <form method="post" action="/settings/command" class="erow"><input type="hidden" name="csrf" value="<CSRF>">
      <input type="hidden" name="provider" value="local-command">
